-- title:
--   Switcheroo Aggregate Fourth Term X Sum
-- statement:
--   **Summing the shared fourth-term factors collapses to the middle sandwich factor.**
--
--   For a fixed slice-pair question `q`, let $X_g$ be the shared fourth-term family indexed by the polynomial `g`. The sum over all polynomial indices equals the outcome sum obtained by inserting the `M` effect on both sides of the complete-part total:
--
--   $$
--   \sum_g X_g
--   =\sum_o M_{q.2,o}\,G_{q.1}^{\mathrm{tot}}\,M_{q.2,o}.
--   $$
--
--   This finite sum identity is the normalization used by both left- and right-action contraction witnesses. It removes the polynomial index before applying the projective submeasurement sandwich bound.
--
--   Formalization credit: Sirui Lu, Ruixuan Deng, Yanqiao Zhu, and Zhengfeng Ji (arXiv:2609.19814). Mathematical source: Zhengfeng Ji, Anand Natarajan, Thomas Vidick, John Wright, and Henry Yuen (arXiv:2009.12982).
--
--   **Formalization Note.** The source declaration is `MIPStarRE.LDT.Pasting.switcherooAggregateFourthTermX_sum`; its Lean statement gives the exact quantifier order and all boundary hypotheses.
